## First-session prompt

Copy this prompt into an agent that has access to this folder:

> Read `AGENTS.md` and initialize yourself with this workspace. Read `_control/PROJECT-RULES.md`, `_control/STATE.md` and `_control/registry/INDEX.md`; verify the actual files before relying on prior conversation context. I want to document the following project: [describe the idea]. Begin conversational discovery, identify what is already known and what remains uncertain, and help me capture the initial vision. Do not bulk-scaffold the catalog or start with a large questionnaire. Keep confirmed facts, proposals, assumptions and open questions distinct. Ask focused questions only when an answer materially changes the project.

## Workspace map

| Location | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [`docs/`](docs/README.md) | Project-specific documents and supporting artifacts. |
| [`_framework/`](_framework/GUIDE.md) | Reusable methodology, rules, templates, defaults and command reference. |
| [`_control/`](_control/STATE.md) | Project configuration, state, phases, approvals, registers and session history. |
| [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) | Compact, framework-managed agent operating contract. |
| [`bp.py`](bp.py) | Cross-platform workspace command launcher. |

The project document inventory is [`_control/registry/MANIFEST.md`](_control/registry/MANIFEST.md), and generated navigation is [`_control/registry/INDEX.md`](_control/registry/INDEX.md). The stakeholder registers are [`DECISIONS.md`](_control/registry/DECISIONS.md), [`ASSUMPTIONS.md`](_control/registry/ASSUMPTIONS.md), [`QUESTIONS.md`](_control/registry/QUESTIONS.md), [`RISKS.md`](_control/registry/RISKS.md) and [`GLOSSARY.md`](_control/registry/GLOSSARY.md).

## Working principles

- The document architecture is adaptive. Choose the smallest set of documents that gives the project adequate coverage; expand or reorganize it when evidence justifies doing so.
- Catalog profile counts are not limits on project document count.
- The owner explicitly accepts decisions and approves individual document versions.
- A clean strict check is necessary for structural confidence but does not establish semantic completeness or architectural correctness.
- The workspace is the durable project record. End each substantive session with an accurate state checkpoint and handoff.

